      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The Electoral College fundamentally distorts democratic representation by granting disproportionate voting power to swing states while effectively disenfranchising voters in large, safe states. This system allows a minority of citizens in populous states to have less influence on the presidency than a majority of citizens in smaller states, directly contradicting the principle of \"one person, one vote.\" By prioritizing strategic states over the actual will of the majority, it creates a two-tiered democracy where the outcome is decided by geography rather than population size.",
      "source": "target",
