      "content": "that's a pretty heavy take on the founders' intentions. but wouldn't someone who believes in federalism say that the US is supposed to be a collection of states rather than just one big mass of people? even if it's not a perfect system, isn't there a legitimate way to defend it as a way to keep a diverse group of states together? it feels like you're saying there's no valid reason to ever support the current structure.",
